<p>Read this sentence: “The candidates who scored highest marks, were selected for the interview.” Does the comma look natural? To most students it does — and that single extra comma has cost marks in SSC CGL, CHSL and bank exams for years.</p>
<p>Punctuation error spotting is the quiet marks-killer. Unlike spelling or vocabulary, punctuation rarely feels “wrong” when you first see it. Your brain fills in the pause and moves on. Examiners know this. They place one misplaced comma, one missing apostrophe or one wrong quotation mark inside an otherwise clean sentence, and the option looks perfect until you apply the rule.</p>
<p>This guide gives you the exact set of punctuation rules that appear again and again in SSC and bank papers, grouped into six clear boxes with memory tricks, real exam-style examples, a quick-reference table, a 5-step checking method and two full practice rounds with answers.</p>

